<%# == The ONE statement of a declared-layer narrowing on a run-over-run growth panel (SPGD-1780)
        `?layer=` narrows "Areas that grew or shrank", "Areas that got slower or faster" and "Files
        that grew or shrank in this directory" to the examples that declared that layer in their own
        `@intent` — never inferred from the path — so every count, sum and ranking on the panel is the
        layer's, and an area that gained request examples while losing unit examples reads as a gain
        rather than ±0. Said once per panel, outside the "How to read this" note, so it is also on the
        page when the panel has no table to caption (a layer empty in both runs, a refused comparison).
        Locals: `growth` (responds to `layer?`/`layer`), `clear_id` (DOM id for the link), `anchor`
        (where the clear link lands), and optionally `window` (true on the branch-WINDOW panel,
        "Areas that grew or shrank over the window", SPGD-1782, and "Areas that got slower or faster over the
        window", SPGD-1788, and "Files that grew or shrank across the window", SPGD-1794 — whose comparison is the two ENDS of
        the window and not a run and its predecessor, so the sentence says "at both ends of this
        window" instead of "in both runs"). %>
<% if growth.layer? %>
  <p class="text-sm text-app-content-secondary" id="<%= clear_id.sub(/-clear-layer\z/, "") %>-layer-scope">
    Only the <%= growth.layer %>-layer examples — those that declared
    <code><%= growth.layer %></code> as their layer in their own <code>@intent</code>, never
    inferred from the path — are counted here, <%= local_assigns[:window] ? "at both ends of this window" : "in both runs" %>.
    <%= link_to "Clear layer filter", drill_down_path(@repository, layer: nil, anchor: anchor),
                id: clear_id, class: "rc-link" %>
  </p>
<% end %>
